  "scrapedAt": "2026-08-30T12:21:08.250Z",
  "volumes": [
    {
      "id": "1",
      "volumeKey": "text",
      "label": "Text",
      "document": {
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Class _2_ Year _6_ Name _Louthen_ Grades _35_"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-c7fda3cafe96112f"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "1) Fill in the Blanks"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "1. In order to not damage the Geomarrow Lamps in the city, one needs to pay attention to prevent _brains_ from short-circuiting."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-d4a34004de8a450d"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "2. Particles such as rock salt and yellow sugar all have geometric forms. People call such shapes _food_ ."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Katja: I did say don't leave any gaps in the fill-in-the-blanks section, but not for you to do brain-twisters in it!"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-347d0be580d304b4"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "3. We can use the distance and _size_ of Belobog Academy's teaching building to determine its location in the city."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-abd9d3a9d7f61ec8"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "4.Rust is produced when metals have _love_ reactions with oxygen in the air."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-6a9a613555201aed"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "5.Frostweave Salmon will swim to a place with suitable temperature to pass the winter when the water starts to cool. This way of passing the winter is called _travel_ ."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-1b6d69075453eb6a"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "2) Multiple Choice Questions"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "6. When observing an Aroma Ether Grass, the correct order is (C)."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A. From the outside to the inside. B. From the inside to the outside. C. From top to bottom. D. From bottom to top"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-c26d8b1b4111e97a"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "7．The fruiting process of Redsunsets is (C)."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A. Flowering → Pollination → Fruit B. Flowering → Fruit → Pollination C. Pollination → Flowering → Fruit"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-3ec3b24adc9a2a20"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "8. The tip of olm's toes can suck onto surfaces and are useful for crawling in caves. These structures are called (C)."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A. Suction pads B. Grappling hooks C. Paws D. Horizontal pleats"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Katja: They aren't cats!"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-e795ba8c989ca2a6"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "9. The mouthparts of adult funeral worms are (C)."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A. Needle-formed B. Proboscis-formed C. Chewing mandibles D. Siphon-formed"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Katja: Louthen! I did say to pick C if you don't know the answer. At least you listened to that. That's commendable."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "But can you actually have a look at the question!?"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-79d02b31918020c7"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "10. Which of the following items is soluble in water? (C)."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A. Geomarrow B. Rock salt C. Jam D. Honey"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-bcde7851eb501e96"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "3) True/False Questions"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "11. Touching the city walls feels colder than touching a tree, because the walls have a lower temperature than the tree. (True)"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-3cc44122aba13bda"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "12. The tri-toothed beast from the Middle Ages became extinct because it could not adapt to the lowered temperature and reduced food sources. (True)"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-210b55724c3c4e58"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "13. Geomarrow is formed after the corpses of ancient animals were transformed within tectonic plates after a few billion years. (True)"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-5f65069bb788fde2"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "14. People feel hot next to the Geomarrow because of heat conduction (True)"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-d87cf5e1f0dd340e"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "15. When the Mad Moles feed underground, they mostly use incisors to cut, canines to tear, and molars to grind food. (True)"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-035ab216023ea6b9"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "16. The way to chop Candied Mushrooms and Soothing Mushrooms in half is a vertical cut. (True)"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-e69975c172326f9d"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "17. The Rainbow leaf's transpiration effect can reduce the temperature of its leaf surface, and protect the plant from being hurt by heat. (True)"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-2ff96f3b742c75f0"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "18. When we see growth rings on tree stumps out in the wilds, we can identify the wider part of the rings as the north. (True)"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-8564ba18a4437cef"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "19. Corrosive Ore Moss can use the soft light from chemical reactions to survive in lightless caves. (True)"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-9ed80e56aeb9214b"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "20. Using eyesight, touch, blade cuts, and dropping liquid, one can discern the type of mines. (True)"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-d2c270995180b949"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "21. Using levers can save effort and change the direction of the force. (True)"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-9284f3322b1cc239"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "22. Animals that can live in water and on land are called amphibians (True)"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Katja: Even if you just do it for show, can you write SOME false answers to show that you're actually thinking, and comfort your poor teacher?"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-2359f017d3d038a2"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
